## Methodology

My approach to the lab followed a simplified security-testing workflow:

1. Understand the target
2. Investigate available services/functionality
3. Identify potential weaknesses
4. Test the identified weakness
5. Validate the result
6. Document the outcome

## Key Takeaway

This was my first practical introduction to thinking like an attacker and applying previously learned computer, networking and web concepts to a security problem.
